# Code hygiene & patterns

## Next.js App Router

### Components
- **Default to Server Components.** Add `"use client"` only for browser APIs, event handlers, or hooks.
- Keep client components small at the leaves; pass data from the server as props.
- Do not import server-only modules (Node APIs, secrets) inside client components.

### Data & routes
- Prefer loading data in `async` Server Components instead of `useEffect` + fetch.
- Use `loading.tsx`, `<Suspense>`, and `error.tsx` when routes need streaming or segment-level errors.
- Route folders: `lowercase-kebab-case`. Groups: `(group-name)` — parentheses exclude the name from the URL. Pages: `page.tsx`, layouts: `layout.tsx`.
- **Non-route folders under `app/`** must use a leading **`_`** so Next.js treats them as private (not URL segments): `app/_components/`, `app/_utils/`, `app/_actions/`, etc. Do not create `app/components/` or `app/utils/` — those would become URL segments.

### Next.js built-ins
- `next/image`, `next/link`, `next/font` for images, internal links, and fonts.

## TypeScript

- `"strict": true` — do not disable.
- Avoid `any`; use `unknown` and narrow.
- Avoid `@ts-ignore` / `@ts-expect-error` without a short comment.

### Path aliases (barrel imports)

**TypeScript path mapping** in [`tsconfig.json`](../../tsconfig.json). Prefer **barrel** entry points:

| Alias | Folder | Import |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `@components` | [`app/_components/index.ts`](../../app/_components/index.ts) | `import { HeroSection } from "@components"` |
| `@utils` | [`app/_utils/index.ts`](../../app/_utils/index.ts) | `import { formatDisplayDate } from "@utils"` |

- Add each new component or util to the folder’s **`index.ts`** (re-export). Implement in named files alongside it (`app/_components/HeroSection.tsx`, `app/_utils/dates.ts`).
- Optional deep imports when needed: `@components/HeroSection`, `@utils/dates` — still prefer the barrel for public API.
- **`@/*`** remains for other roots (`@/app/_actions/…`) if useful.
- **Do not** use these aliases for npm packages (`react`, `next`, `@radix-ui/…`, etc.).

Colocated route files may use `./` (e.g. `./globals.css` in `app/layout.tsx`).

## Environment variables

- Never expose secrets with the `NEXT_PUBLIC_` prefix.
- Do not commit `.env` or `.env.local`. Document new variable **names** in `.env.example` when they exist.

## Shared code

- UI → `app/_components/` (export via `@components`). Pure helpers → `app/_utils/` (export via `@utils`).

## Naming

| Thing | Convention | Example |
|---|---|---|
| Route segment | `lowercase-kebab-case` | `privacy-policy/` |
| Non-route folder under `app/` | `_` prefix | `_components/`, `_actions/` |
| React component file | `PascalCase.tsx` | `HeroSection.tsx` |
| Utility file | `camelCase.ts` | `formatHours.ts` |

## General hygiene

- No commented-out code or stray `console.log` in merged work.
- One main concern per file when possible.

### Import order

Enforced by Biome **Organize Imports** on save / pre-commit ([`biome.json`](../../biome.json)). Blank lines separate groups; **sources are sorted A→Z within each group** (lexicographic); named imports inside `{ … }` are sorted the same way.

| Group | Examples |
| --- | --- |
| 1. Node / Bun built-ins | `node:fs`, `node:path`, `bun:test` |
| 2. React & Next.js | `react`, `react-dom`, `next/*` (framework before other npm deps) |
| 3. Other npm packages | `clsx`, `server-only`, etc. |
| 4. Project aliases | `@components`, `@utils`, `@/*` (before npm — not scoped packages) |
| 5. Relative modules | `./foo`, `../bar` |
| 6. Styles last | `./globals.css`, `*.module.css` (`:STYLE:`) |

Use **Organize Imports** (or `pnpm format`) instead of hand-sorting. `import type` stays in the same group as its module.

